      "text": "he that endureth to the end, Matt. 10:22 (24:13; Mark 13:13). harvest is the end of the world, Matt. 13:39. at the end of the world … sever the wicked, Matt. 13:49. sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world, Matt. 24:3 (JS—M 1:4). end is not yet, Matt. 24:6 (Mark 13:7; Luke 21:9; JS—M 1:23). preached … unto all nations; and then shall the end come, Matt. 24:14 (JS—M 1:31). I am with you alway, even unto the end, Matt. 28:20 (D&C 24:8). of his kingdom there shall be no end, Luke 1:33. he loved them unto the end, John 13:1. supper being ended, the devil … into the heart of Judas, John 13:2. To this end was I born, John 18:37. Christ is the end of the law for righteousness, Rom. 10:4. upon whom the ends of the world are come, 1 Cor. 10:11. whose end shall be according to their works, 2 Cor. 11:15. throughout all ages, world without end, Eph. 3:21. Whose end is destruction, Philip. 3:19. neither beginning of days, nor end of life, Heb. 7:3 (Alma 13:7). in the end of the world hath he appeared to put away, Heb. 9:26. end of your faith, even the salvation, 1 Pet. 1:9. what shall the end be of them that obey not, 1 Pet. 4:17. latter end is worse, 2 Pet. 2:20. Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end, Rev. 21:6.",
